//!
//! `Ensemble`: the whole forest of 300 trees on-chain in one call, to measure what a dispute
//! saves. The trees do not fit one contract's code (76800 bytes of tree words), so the holders
//! `Trees0` .. `Trees4` each keep a slice of at most 64 trees and walk it; `Ensemble` asks
//! each for its slice's outputs, joins them and adds them up with `Outputs::scores`, the
//! function the class challenge runs. Every tree is walked by `Tree::eval`, the function a tree
//! challenge runs.
